      }
    ],
    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 152,
        "text": "So, team, thanks for coming. Let's look at the new city traffic data. Our question is simple: does the new bike lane on King Street reduce car use?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "93f5d57fe70d1bca73c3591f8fa88224ee80b44ef12c6c7bca9e784e23881127",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 159,
        "sourceEnd": 284,
        "text": "I pulled the numbers this morning. Car trips on King Street dropped by 18 percent after the lane opened. That's a big change.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "d81f3becebdb8dffde0e4371022505a0e1ed21988b062e3204a7ead7f0f34ae2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 291,
        "sourceEnd": 430,
        "text": "It is. But wait — car trips on Queen Street also dropped by 15 percent, and there's no bike lane there. So something else may be happening.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "e6847437feb85aef2dd360071e7c7a0920ae193be5df9cd6ca0e75a4fa5a1390",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 437,
        "sourceEnd": 587,
        "text": "Good point. Maybe more people are working from home this year. The city survey says remote work rose from 12 percent to 27 percent in the same period.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "415c29bfdef7c4da7a2c34fbfbc32e9692a5dee1e941c82b542ec0e6dcc33937",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 594,
        "sourceEnd": 734,
        "text": "Exactly. So the bike lane and the drop in car trips are correlated, but we can't say the lane caused the drop. Correlation is not causation.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "28e478432f20f29565c3f01f49f2206911dae82128d7d7e837dae40086b40179",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 741,
        "sourceEnd": 860,
        "text": "Right. To test cause, we need a comparison group. Queen Street can be our comparison group because it has no bike lane.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "451679a7f8c4c1d8f87355c47124dd4003932e4a8b59cd70acd15651431e5677",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 867,
        "sourceEnd": 1025,
        "text": "Perfect. Now, what about bus use? On King Street, bus trips were 2.5 times higher than before the lane. On Queen Street, bus trips were only 1.2 times higher.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "efdf90eeb99996015c345a89d7e013fe34271e9024385d2c4c9e0a670663a3f6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1032,
        "sourceEnd": 1131,
        "text": "So the increase on King Street is more than twice the increase on Queen Street. That's interesting.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "350ecd0675cd2c71bfd20e87a42805399f9c293592599e9231d504c7a539f8c0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1138,
        "sourceEnd": 1294,
        "text": "Yes. But we still need to check other factors. For example, the city added two new bus routes on King Street last year. That could explain the bus increase.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "e1ecd5042b767ce9d9fcb45486310567e1a11ffdecde5e0f0c1ed06c083af793",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1301,
        "sourceEnd": 1374,
        "text": "True. So for buses, the new routes might be the cause, not the bike lane.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "b894a9accb9093541eba08a18f017c0d4f7e6c3417135a600fcb5ce163440f2c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1381,
        "sourceEnd": 1508,
        "text": "Let's write this down. We have three possible causes: the bike lane, remote work, and new bus routes. We need to separate them.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "164b375e3a53552854ba26c3780034876816df8f1212ee8f0f96e1a19e0a0b01",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1515,
        "sourceEnd": 1696,
        "text": "How about a simple chart? We can show car trips before and after on both streets. King Street: 10,000 car trips per day before, 8,200 after. Queen Street: 9,000 before, 7,650 after.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "18dfa5e1fff54b38de6c179921e0c595cedb07c1a3af80e0f802653d8bccc672",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1703,
        "sourceEnd": 1834,
        "text": "Good. So King Street dropped by 1,800 trips, and Queen Street dropped by 1,350 trips. The King Street drop is bigger, but not huge.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "d5afd83cbe689b1a542decc2cc2a669906e4146ac8fe7dcf5a2d06514ea52829",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1841,
        "sourceEnd": 1972,
        "text": "And the percentage drop is 18 percent on King Street and 15 percent on Queen Street. So the difference is only 3 percentage points.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "2265934eb8a469f0518274735d29803b59e27058879040addcccbccaeddf9746",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1979,
        "sourceEnd": 2086,
        "text": "That's small. It suggests the bike lane may not be the main cause. Remote work is probably a bigger factor.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "1549dbb223d1ac29ff190babafbc4fe4a36e20b6ef3f7cca555c31c7c1bbefa9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2093,
        "sourceEnd": 2135,
        "text": "Should we say the bike lane had no effect?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "2cdc3889315683fc7c170d5a7931aee1e934826ae8198c87eeaeec29793d79d1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2142,
        "sourceEnd": 2298,
        "text": "No, we can't say that either. We just don't have enough evidence. We need a controlled study. For now, we can say the data shows a correlation, not a cause.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "f0b06b690acb56ab60690223a2c761aa8e4adc595aff38a1c48ecc0ba375a1ec",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2305,
        "sourceEnd": 2487,
        "text": "Got it. So our report will say: car trips fell on both streets, but the fall was similar. The bike lane is one possible factor, but remote work and new bus routes are also important.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "8f6eb40bbcde5105445acd0df813c39cda07a6439a86f4ce57865d1c2bda236d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2494,
        "sourceEnd": 2587,
        "text": "Exactly. And we should use careful language: 'may be associated with' instead of 'caused by'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "35a6a234edb109188dd478c36f9e024108a48ba4fd0f244dfe69cb94af95ee11",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 2594,
        "sourceEnd": 2669,
        "text": "Agreed. I'll make the chart with before and after numbers for both streets.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "97e15e390390904d3d5b98446e2d51c5d8204b2264f1c38d7c87321cd73704c3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2676,
        "sourceEnd": 2730,
        "text": "Great. Let's meet again on Friday to review the draft.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "b476cbe0238694c6c2c7f4cbd49f89557c8bd36b9d70faf7b1f597ae4fd7651e",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
